18#,#18 Major (Applied)#,#Applied Mathematics#,#Bachelor of Science in Mathematics (Applied Mathematics Option)

Applied mathematics focuses on the mathematical concepts and techniques applied in science, engineering, and computer science. Particular attention is given to the following principles and their mathematical formulations: propagation, equilibrium, stability, optimization, computation, statistics, and random processes.

required_subjects

restricted_electives

communication


%% Required Subjects
required_subjects, "Required Subjects" := (18.03/18.032/18.152/18.303), (18.04/18.112), 18.06, 18.300, (18.200/18.200A)

%% Group I: Probability and statistics, combinatorics, computer science
%% Based on MIT Math department Applied Mathematics option requirements (https://math.mit.edu/academics/undergrad/major/course18/applied.html)
group_i, "Group I: Probability, Statistics, Combinatorics, Computer Science" := 18.204/18.211/18.212/18.400/18.404/18.410/18.424/18.434/18.453/18.600/18.650

%% Group II: Numerical analysis, physical mathematics, nonlinear dynamics
%% Based on MIT Math department Applied Mathematics option requirements (https://math.mit.edu/academics/undergrad/major/course18/applied.html)
group_ii, "Group II: Numerical Analysis, Physical Mathematics, Nonlinear Dynamics" := 18.303/18.330/18.352/18.353/18.354/18.384

%% Restricted Electives: Select 4 courses with at least 1 from each group
restricted_electives, "Restricted Electives" := group_i, group_ii{>=4|>=1}

%% Communication-Intensive Subjects: Select 2 from the following
communication, "Communication-Intensive Subjects" := 18.104/18.204/18.384/18.424/18.434/18.504/18.704/18.784/18.821/18.904/18.994/8.06/14.18/14.33/18.100P/18.100Q/18.200{>=2}
